          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On November 12, 1977, at approximately 4:53 PM, two individuals observed in the sky a bright, elongated object that was initially stationary, then gradually ascended into the air before disappearing instantly into the clouds. No unusual noises were heard during the observation, which lasted over twenty seconds. No particular military maneuvers were conducted at the military base that day. These witnesses likely observed the passage of a sunlit weather balloon.",
